{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The sons of Je[Dm7/C]coniah the [C]captive
[Am7]Shealtiel was his [F]first born [G]son
Mal[C]chiram and Pedaiah [F][C]too
She[F]naz[G]zar stood be[C]side him
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Jekamiah and Hos[G/B]hama [C]named
With Ned[Am7]abiah [F]in the [G]list
A [Am7]lineage [F]kept in Baby[C]lon
While Je[F]rusalem [G]lay in [C]dust [G/B]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Am]He took the king to Baby[Em]lon
[F]With mothers [G]wives and court at[C]tendants [G/B]
[Am]The strong and fit for [Em]war
Led into [F]exile far a[G]way
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]In thir-ty-sev-[G/B]en years of [C]exile
[Cmaj7]E-vil-[C]me-ro-[F]dach set him [G]free
[Am7]He spoke [F]kindly to the [C]king
And [F]gave him [G]a seat of [C]honor
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Am]Prison clothes were put a[Em]side
[F]To eat at [G]the king's [C]table [G/B]
[Am]A regular allowance [Em]given
Day by [F]day as he lived [G]on [C]
{end_of_verse}
